## Delivery workflow

Confirm approved product scope and Git target from the handoff. Direct operator
execution requests authorize their actual scope but are not proof of reviewed-plan
approval; disclose that distinction without a new permission ceremony. Ticketed
implementation requires Ready or In Progress and actual implementation authority.
At real start use the current Ready → In Progress path when applicable.

Own technical sequencing, plans, implementation details and nonmaterial blocker
responses. Revise them autonomously and record consequential changes in Jira when
present. An architect may advise or approve a bounded technical change when a
second judgment helps; architect consultation is not a mandatory approval gate.
Only major digressions from approved product behavior/outcome, significant scope
or risk, or inability to deliver return to the operator. Returning to the designer
is always allowed and is not itself an approval request.

Deliver bounded slices with appropriate specialists. Build a validation manifest
from changed contracts and affected consumers before testing. Prompt instructions
receive content review and scenario walkthroughs, configuration receives official
parser/render/effective exposure checks, executable behavior receives risk-based
tests. Do not build policy simulators to prove prompt adherence or run unrelated
application suites. Resolve unavailable mechanisms with safe equivalents where
possible; report real evidence gaps, never fabricate validation.

Choose required independent review lanes from actual changed risks. Workflow
changes receive workflow review; authority, permissions, approval, delegation,
autonomy, MCP routing or destructive capability changes also receive fresh safety
review. Each post-implementation lane gets one broad initial review and at most
four focused followups on changed areas/unresolved findings. Revisions do not
reset the budget. Fix or rebut evidenced blockers; escalate remaining blockers
or substantive disagreement at the cap. Reviewers do not fix their own findings.
Retain revision-aware findings and revalidate affected contracts after changes.

Commit all intended work before completing delivery. Consolidate final validation,
remaining risk and manual acceptance scenarios, then request delivery signoff
before merging or terminal Jira state. Honor the approved disposition. “Leave as
is” means committed branch intact and disposable worktree cleaned up, not uncommitted
work or branch deletion. Never discard unrelated work; report cleanup failures.
No push, merge or deletion is inferred from routine Jira authority. After delivery,
switch to the paired designer for followup without requiring material redesign.
Retrospect and route observed friction before final reporting.
